OpenWings patch 0029: no sign in page for a browser on this computer

OPENWINGS_SIGN_IN=off in .env removes the sign in page. Accounts stay on
(AUTH_ENABLED=true), so chats, settings and connected accounts still belong
to the admin and every feature that needs a signed-in person keeps working.
wings/entrypoint.sh sets WINGS_SIGN_IN_OFF=1 only while the app port is
published on 127.0.0.1 (APP_BIND) and the https profile is off; otherwise it
says so in the log and sign in stays on.

  * app.py: when WINGS_SIGN_IN_OFF=1, installs wings.local_guard.
    LocalOnlyGuard (an OpenWings file, not part of this diff) outside every
    other middleware. The guard refuses any source but the container itself
    and the gateway of one of its Docker networks (where the published port
    delivers from; the code runner, browser and renderer containers and any
    unknown address are refused), any request through a proxy, any Host but
    localhost, 127.0.0.1 or [::1] (DNS rebinding), and any change or
    websocket from another website (Origin must match; Sec-Fetch-Site
    cross-site or same-site is refused, and for /api unless it is a top
    level page load, so sign in returns from providers still work). A page
    load from the published port without a valid session gets a new admin
    session, the same cookie a sign in sets.

